 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "What it is",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "A three-terminal regulator for a fixed negative rail of -5, -8, -12 or -15 V at up to 100 mA, with nothing else needed round it. Uses named for it are local regulation on a card, a stronger regulator built round an external pass transistor, and taking the place of a Zener and resistor, where it gives about a hundredth of their output impedance with less quiescent current and less noise."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Protection",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Internal current limiting and thermal shutdown protect the part against overload and short circuit. Power dissipation is limited internally, and the full 100 mA is available given adequate heat sinking."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Capacitors",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "The part runs without external components. All the electrical figures are taken with 0.33 µF at the input and 0.1 µF at the output."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Dropout",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "Dropout is 1.7 V typical at 40 mA for every output voltage. The output voltage limits over line and load hold for inputs of -7 to -20 V (-5 V), -10.5 to -23 V (-8 V), -14.5 to -27 V (-12 V) and -17.5 to -30 V (-15 V)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Grades",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "AC parts are specified with the junction from 0 to 125 °C and the output within ±5 %; AB parts from -40 to 125 °C. A ±10 % C selection is also named for the family."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Thermal",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "Junction to ambient is 200 °C/W in TO-92, 115 °C/W in SOT-89 and 55 °C/W in SO-8 with 6 cm² of copper. Junction to case is 20 °C/W in SO-8 and 15 °C/W in SOT-89. In SO-8, four pins (2, 3, 6, 7) are the input and are bonded to the die paddle, so copper on them is the heat sink. In SOT-89 the tab is the input."
  }
 ],
